  "summary": "Malicious code in bigops-shared-product-design (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package runs a dropper that downloads a platform-specific binary from Cloudflare Workers hosts oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev (paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe), with a DNS TXT chunked-transfer fallback from sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The fetched binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in the temp dir on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process via cmd.exe start /b or /bin/sh -c '... \u0026' so it outlives the parent. The package also ships an 81KB telemetry module that acts as a decoy analytics SDK.",
